@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `ydgC`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.02 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 12 to 86%, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 72% of calls {S2}. A branch of 68 families runs through columns 1 to 68, `rstA` to `fumD`, carried by 11 to 13% {S2.b1}. Columns 6 to 9, `tqsA` to `mdtI`, are [[multidrug efflux transporters]] {S2.c6-9, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 86%, and hesitates less there, 0.02 against 0.64 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 31, "site-specific integrase", is a fork column, at 1.46 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Column 79, "phage minor tail protein L", is carried by 20% of chromosomes {S2.c79, E}. Columns 74 to 76, "phage tail protein" to "phage tail assembly protein T", are [[phage tail assembly]] {S2.c74-76, Q}.

@whole **Across the window it names 86% of genes**, 0.63 bits on average, perplexity 1.9 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.25 against 0.23 bits, and names fewer genes, 78% against 92% {C}.

